{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "IS281B-N-AXW",
 "kind": "optocoupler",
 "manufacturer": "ISOMICRON",
 "title": "IS281X-N series (IS281A-N, IS281B-N, IS281C-N, IS281D-N): phototransistor optocoupler, DC input, 3750 Vrms, SSOP4",
 "source": {
  "revision": "Rev V01, 2023/07/27",
  "pages": 13
 },
 "summary": "A single-channel optocoupler: an AlGaAs infrared LED on the input side shines on a silicon planar phototransistor, with collector and emitter on their own pins, in a 4-lead SSOP4 body built with a coplanar double mold. The four grades differ only in current transfer ratio at IF = 5 mA, VCE = 5 V: A 80-160 %, B 130-260 %, C 200-400 %, D 300-600 %. Isolation is rated 3750 Vrms for one minute, the collector-emitter rating is 80 V and the part runs from -40 °C to 110 °C. Approvals listed are UL1577, VDE EN60747-5-5 (VDE0884-5) and CQC GB4943.1.",
