   "text": "The letter after 281 is the CTR bin at IF = 5 mA, VCE = 5 V and 25 °C: A 80-160 %, B 130-260 %, C 200-400 %, D 300-600 %."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Response-time definitions",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "With a square current pulse at the input the collector voltage falls and then recovers. tr is the time for the output to move from the 90 % to the 10 % level after the input steps on, and ton the time from the input step to the 10 % level. tf is the time for the output to move from the 10 % to the 90 % level after the input steps off, and toff the time from the input step to the 90 % level."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Derating",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Forward current is 60 mA up to about 95 °C ambient and falls to 30 mA at 110 °C. Collector power dissipation is 150 mW up to about 74 °C and falls to about 45 mW at 110 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 12,
   "text": "One soldering pass is recommended for every method, and IR reflow is limited to three passes. Wave soldering to JESD22-A111 uses two waves: preheat from 25 °C to 140 °C at +2 °C/s over 30 s to 80 s, a rise to the solder at +200 °C/s, the solder at 260 +0/-5 °C for 10 s, then cooling at -5 °C/s. Dipping the body in solder paste is not recommended. Soldering, reflow or long service can discolour the package surface, with no effect on performance or reliability. MSL class 1."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Applications named",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Household appliances, office equipment, programmable controllers and switching power supplies."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Use restrictions",
   "page": 13,
   "text": "The part is not meant for automotive, aircraft, military, medical or life-sustaining equipment, or any use where a failure can injure or kill."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Compliance",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "REACH compliant, halogen free, RoHS and lead-free marks; approvals UL1577, VDE EN60747-5-5 (VDE0884-5) and CQC GB4943.1."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Typical curves",
   "page": 13,
   "text": "The characteristic curves are typical performance and are not guaranteed."
  }
